guile_cpp, vendored in TeXmacs
==============================

guile_cpp is GNU Guile 1.8.8 rewritten in C++ by PikachuHy: a tagged value
representation, a mark-and-sweep collector which scans the C stack
conservatively, a CEK evaluator and a bytecode compiler with its VM, and the
library of libguile 1.8 (numbers with their own bignums, strings, ports,
modules, GOOPS, SRFIs...). It boots the unmodified Scheme library of Guile
1.8.8 (ice-9/boot-9.scm...).

Origin:   https://github.com/PikachuHy/guile_cpp
Commit:   cd6c4b5c6df9ef22d8fc96190a0d879adaafee6a (27 November 2026)
Author:   PikachuHy <pikachuhy@163.com>
License:  pending with its author (guile_cpp is derived from Guile 1.8.8,
          LGPL 2.1 or later; the Scheme files of share/ keep their GNU
          notices). TeXmacs packages must not ship it until it is settled.

The interface of TeXmacs (the tmscm functions) is ../guile_cpp_tm.cpp and
../guile_cpp_tm.hpp. Configure TeXmacs with --with-scheme=guile_cpp (macOS
and Linux only: guile_cpp uses POSIX headers; the browser cannot scan its C
stack). The Scheme side is the one of Guile 1.8: TeXmacs/progs/init-guile.scm.

What is kept
------------

src/                the sources of libguile_cpp, without main.cpp (the guile
                    command line) and jit_arm64.cpp (see below)
include/guile_cpp/  its headers
share/guile/1.8/    the Scheme library (ice-9, oop, srfi), without the
                    Makefile.am of Guile; `make` copies it into
                    TeXmacs/boot/guile_cpp (target GUILE_CPP_DATA of
                    src/Makefile.in), where guile_cpp_tm.cpp finds it from
                    TEXMACS_PATH, so that the packages are relocatable

Not kept: the CMake build, the tests (tests/, test-suite/), the benchmarks,
the README of the project.

Building
--------

The sources are compiled by src/src/makefile.in as Objects/gcpp_<name>.o
(some names are those of sources of TeXmacs, list.cpp, so that this folder
is also left out of the vpath of the makefile), with the flags of TeXmacs:
C++17 and -O2 (guile_cpp itself is built with -O3 by its CMake). Only the
objects of src/Scheme/guile_cpp see the include folder: the rest of TeXmacs
includes include/guile_cpp/value.hpp alone, through guile_cpp_tm.hpp.

Changes to guile_cpp
--------------------

* C++17 instead of C++20: include/guile_cpp/compat.hpp replaces <bit>
  (gcpp_countr_zero, gcpp_countl_zero, gcpp_popcount, gcpp_bit_ceil, with
  the results of the standard functions for 0) and the attributes
  [[likely]] / [[unlikely]] of the if and while statements
  (GCPP_LIKELY / GCPP_UNLIKELY, with __builtin_expect).
* No JIT: jit_arm64.cpp (the ARM64 compiler of macOS) is not compiled; its
  calls in bytecode.cpp are under #ifdef GUILE_CPP_JIT, which TeXmacs never
  defines, and VM::jit_enabled is false by default.
* include/guile_cpp/value.hpp: the tagged values (SCM), the header of the
  heap objects (Obj, ObjTag), the pairs and is_pair, is_symbol, is_string,
  moved out of scm.hpp, which includes it.
* load.cpp: the directories of the Scheme library are given at run time
  (set_data_dirs, called before VM::init), instead of the paths compiled in
  by the CMake build (GUILE_CPP_PKGDATA_DIR...), which remain the defaults
  when they are defined.
